<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Viva Maria uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1799</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Viva Maria was a popular uprising against the French occupation of Tuscany in 1799, which began in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arezzo">Arezzo</a> in May under the cry 'Viva Maria'. Peasant bands led by local notables and clergy drove out the French and their Jacobin supporters and occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> and Siena, where they massacred members of the Jewish community. The bands were dissolved after the Austrians arrived, and the French returned after their victory at Marengo in 1800.</p></div>
